# security/signing.env.example -- template for the signed-manifest integrity
# system. Copy to security/signing.env (gitignored/private -- never publish
# your fingerprint's associated real manifest/signature alongside a public
# fork) and fill in YOUR OWN key.
#
# 1. Generate a signing key if you don't have one:
#      gpg --full-generate-key   (ed25519 recommended)
# 2. Get its fingerprint:
#      gpg --fingerprint <your-email-or-name>
# 3. Put that fingerprint below.
# 4. Export your public key so verify-manifest.sh can check signatures
#    without depending on your ambient keyring's trust state:
#      gpg --armor --export <fingerprint> > security/trusted-signing-key.pub.asc
# 5. Run scripts/sign-manifest.sh to generate + sign MANIFEST.sha256 for
#    your own copy of this repo.
SIGNING_KEY_FINGERPRINT=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
